.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-DELETE-ROLE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-delete-role \- delete one of your account's roles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eam delete-role
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a role from your account.
.SH IT IS REFUSED WHILE ANYTHING STILL GRANTS IT
A role that is still named by a grant cannot be deleted. Revoke those
grants first;
.B euclid-cli eam list-grants --role <name>
lists them and
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-role (1)
removes each one.
.PP
Refused rather than cascading, and deliberately. A grant names its role
rather than copying it, so deleting the role out from under its grants
would leave grants that quietly do nothing \- present in every listing,
granting nothing, and failing only when somebody is turned away from
something they were told they had. Taking somebody's access away is a
decision worth making on purpose, one grant at a time.
.PP
The error says how many grants are in the way.
.SH BUILT-IN ROLES CANNOT BE DELETED
.IR account\-administrator ,
.IR operator ,
.IR reader ,
.IR publisher ,
.IR consumer ,
.I application
and
.I transfer
are computed rather than stored \- there is nothing to delete. See
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-roles (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Role name. Must be one of your account's own roles. Required.
.SH WHO MAY RUN IT
Installation administrators \- members of the
.I administrator
user group. See
.B ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES
in
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The role was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
No name given, no role of that name in your account, a built-in name, a
grant still names it, or the caller is not an administrator. If the
failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored
credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
Retire a role, grants first:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-grants \e
    --role order-service

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam revoke-role \e
    --grant-id 7c1f2f5e-3a21-4e6b-9a0c-5f2b9e1d4c33

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-role \e
    --name order-service
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-grants (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-roles (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-update-role (1)
